<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jie people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jie were a non-Chinese people of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the 4th century, probably of Central Asian origin and associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> confederation, settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a>. Their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-le">Shi Le</a> founded the Later Zhao state, which dominated northern China. In 350 the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ran-min">Ran Min</a> ordered the massacre of the Jie in Ye, and they disappear as a distinct people soon afterwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jie-people.jpg" alt="Jie people" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sixteen_Kingdoms_338_AD_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
